      'Certified means a third-party or internal program stamp that a recovery/continuity program exists or once met a named checklist (ISO/SOC/DR cert, annual auditor letter, laminated "certified recoverable" badge) — not the same as risk transfer that pays when restore fails under today’s named owner inside the named window. It is not insured. Insured means a named, in-force indemnity/coverage instrument (policy, binder, endorsement, named insured + limits + triggers + exclusions + claims path) that actually responds when recovery fails or loss lands — not a certificate PDF, not a sales claim that "we’re covered," and not a CMMS checkbox. A firm can be certified and still not insured. A firm can be insured and still not certified. A certificate alone is not insurance. A policy alone is not certification. A CMMS checkbox, ticket state, status light, or one-off clear is neither.',
