    relatedSlug: 'successor-accepted-is-not-sustained',
    relatedNote: 'Accepted is not sustained. Accepted means under that same named instrument / governing law for that channel, instrument-required acceptance that accepts the restored successor-obligation outcome for the named successor return-to-service bar across the next named acceptance / remaining-obligation / warranty / control window — evidenced by acceptance package with named stakeholder / owner / ops acceptor roles, named acceptance criteria met (restoration package cited, next acceptance window named, return-to-service bar the restoration must meet stated, residual ownership still named), dates, and an unbroken trail from the restoration evidence to that acceptance evidence — not a dashboard green tile with no acceptance authority, not a verbal "we accepted it," not extending an acceptance memo with no instrument path, not a chat note that says accepted, not "ops will sign the release" without instrument-required acceptance evidence, and not treating restoration theater as automatic acceptance of that restored successor-obligation outcome. Sustained means under that same named instrument / governing law for that channel, instrument-required sustainment that holds the accepted successor-obligation outcome in evidenced continuity under real operating load across the next named sustain / remaining-obligation / warranty / control window — evidenced by sustainment package with named sustainer / owner roles, named sustainment criteria met (acceptance package cited, next sustain window named, operating-load continuity the acceptance must hold stated, residual ownership still named), dates, and an unbroken trail from the acceptance evidence to that sustainment evidence — not a dashboard green tile with no sustainment authority, not a verbal "we sustained it," not extending a sustain memo with no instrument path, not a chat note that says sustained, not "ops will keep it running" without instrument-required sustainment evidence, and not treating acceptance theater as automatic sustainment of that accepted successor-obligation outcome. A dashboard green tile with no sustainment authority, a verbal "we sustained it," extending a sustain memo with no instrument path, a chat note that says sustained, or "ops will keep it running" without instrument-required sustainment evidence is not that sustainment. This sustained is successor-obligation sustainment of the accepted outcome under real operating load across the named sustain window in the industrial control and transfer spine. It is not the filing-spine holding of an accepted restored condition in Accepted Is Not Sustained, and it is not the sustainment of an operated successor-obligation outcome in Operated Is Not Sustained.',
